=== SURVEY ===
- Hook: useTeslaEnergyLiveStatus(siteId) from @/api/hooks/useEnergy
  Returns TeslaEnergyLiveStatus with fields: solar_power, battery_power, load_power, grid_power (watts, nullable)
- Hook: useTeslaEnergySites() — discovers site IDs
- Shared component: WidgetFlowDiagram from ./shared — handles diamond SVG layout, animated arrows, compact mode
- WidgetFlowDiagram accepts FlowNode[] (id, label, value, formattedValue, icon, position) and FlowArrow[] (from, to, value, active, color)
- SolarProductionWidget used as pattern reference for energy site hooks + WidgetShell freshness props

=== REASONING ===
- Four nodes: Solar (top), Grid (left), Home (right), Battery (bottom) — matches diamond layout positions in WidgetFlowDiagram
- Power values from API are in watts; convert to kW for display (÷1000)
- Arrow direction logic:
  - Solar → Home when solar_power > 0
  - Solar → Battery when solar producing AND battery charging (battery_power > 0)
  - Battery → Home when discharging (battery_power < 0)
  - Grid → Home when importing (grid_power > 0)
  - Home → Grid when exporting (grid_power < 0)
  - Grid → Battery when battery charging from grid (battery_power > 0, no solar)
- No unit conversion needed (kW is universal, not distance/temp/pressure)
- Compact mode (cols <= 1) delegated to WidgetFlowDiagram which truncates labels and limits arrows
- All strings via useTranslation('dashboard')
- Null-safe: liveStatus?.solar_power ?? 0, (sites ?? [])[0]?.energy_site_id

